{"acceptedResponses":["B"],"answer":"B","bank":"amc","batch":"NA","choiceOrder":["A","B","C","D","E"],"choices":{"A":"\\(-\\dfrac12\\)","B":"\\(-1\\)","C":"\\(\\dfrac12\\)","D":"\\(1\\)","E":"undetermined"},"choicesType":"text","domain":[],"editorialNote":"","figureSources":{},"id":"1968_AMC_12_Q13","knowledgeGraph":{"assessedIds":["cnm_039"],"contentHash":"046464228a6606b877cacf921448827cd8f6ef117bd1458683b2643082f773d8","flags":[],"reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"self-referential-vieta-relations","label":"Apply root-coefficient relations","methodDirectNodeIds":{"self-referential-vieta-relations":["cnm_226"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_226"]},{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"substitute-the-nonzero-root","label":"Substitute n as a root","methodDirectNodeIds":{"substitute-the-nonzero-root":["cnm_039","cnm_151"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_039","cnm_151"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_029","cnm_040","cnm_150"],"id":"substitute-root","label":"Use the meaning of a root","methodDirectNodeIds":{"substitute-root":["cnm_039","cnm_151"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_039","cnm_151","cnm_029","cnm_040","cnm_150"]}],"status":"mapped","supportIds":["cnm_029","cnm_040","cnm_150"],"version":"1.0.0"},"level":"AMC 12","number":13,"question":"If \\(m\\) and \\(n\\) are the roots of \\(x^2+mx+n=0,\\) \\(m\\ne0,\\) \\(n\\ne0,\\) then the sum of the roots is:","questionType":"text","rejectedAnswers":[],"responseType":"choice","schemaVersion":"3.0","skill":[],"solution":"Because \\(n\\) is itself a root, substituting \\(x=n\\) gives an equation containing the sum we want:\n\\[\nn^2+mn+n=0.\n\\]\nFactor out \\(n\\):\n\\[\nn(n+m+1)=0.\n\\]\nSince \\(n\\ne0\\), division by \\(n\\) is valid, giving \\(n+m+1=0\\). Thus the sum of the roots is \\(m+n=-1\\).\n\nThe conditions are consistent: \\(m=1\\) and \\(n=-2\\) give \\(x^2+x-2=(x-1)(x+2)\\), whose roots are precisely \\(1\\) and \\(-2\\). The requested sum is therefore \\(\\boxed{-1}\\), choice B.","solutionAvailability":"present","solutionMe